# Always-On Memory Architecture

## Overview

Little Nate has **Total Recall** — semantic memory search runs on EVERY user message at zero cost via Cloudflare Vectorize. This replaces the old intent-gated approach where memory only activated when specific keywords were detected.

## Architecture (Patent-Pending: Multi-Surface Semantic Recall)

```
User Message
 ↓
always_on_memory_recall() [zero cost — Cloudflare Vectorize]
 ↓ queries 6 indexes concurrently (topK=30 each)
 ├── nate-memory-search (conversations)
 ├── nate-vault-search (vault files)
 ├── nate-wisdom (wisdom extractions)
 ├── nate-me2me (identity patterns)
 ├── nate-sessions (session notes)
 └── nate-annotations (photo analyses)
 ↓ filters by relevance threshold (score > 0.30)
 ↓ caps at 25 results
 ↓ injects as memory_search_context
process_interaction()
```

## Two Memory Modes

| Mode | Trigger | Scope | Sources |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Always-On** | Every message | Vectorize semantic only | 6 vector indexes |
| **Deep Search** | Intent keywords or explicit request | Full unified_search | PostgreSQL FTS + ILIKE + vault + annotations + device local + Vectorize |

The always-on mode is lightweight and fast (one embedding + 6 parallel vector queries). Deep search activates when the user explicitly asks to search ("find my photo", "search my history", etc.).

## Key Parameters

| Parameter | Value | Location | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|
| `RELEVANCE_THRESHOLD` | 0.30 | `always_on_memory_recall()` | Filters noise; vectors below this score are irrelevant |
| `TOP_K_PER_INDEX` | 30 | `always_on_memory_recall()` | Broader recall per index; was 10 |
| `MAX_RESULTS_TO_LLM` | 25 | `always_on_memory_recall()` | Prevents context overflow |
| Conversation truncation | 600 chars | `format_search_context()` | Was 200; allows richer context |
| Photo analysis truncation | 2000 chars | `format_search_context()` | Was 1200; full AI descriptions |
| Vault preview | 400 chars | `format_search_context()` | Was 200; more detail visible |
| `unified_search` results cap | `limit * 2` | `unified_search()` | Accounts for Vectorize additions |

## Entity Extraction at Capture

Every `memorize()` call runs `_extract_entities()` on the combined user + AI text. This extracts:

| Category | Examples | Stored In |
|---|---|---|
| colors | red, blue, gold, navy | `metadata.entities.colors` |
| clothing | shirt, dress, hat, watch | `metadata.entities.clothing` |
| people | mom, dad, friend, boss | `metadata.entities.people` |
| places | home, work, church, park | `metadata.entities.places` |
| emotions | happy, anxious, overwhelmed | `metadata.entities.emotions` |
| topics | relationship, trauma, career | `metadata.entities.topics` |
| temporal | yesterday, last year, childhood | `metadata.entities.temporal` |

These entities are stored in the `metadata` JSONB column of `conversation_history` and indexed via Vectorize for precision recall.

## System Prompt Additions

Two new guidelines added to Nate's system prompt:

1. **TOTAL RECALL** — instructs Nate to weave recalled memories naturally into responses
2. **PRECISION MEMORY** — instructs Nate to search for exact detail matches (colors, clothing, objects)

## Rules

1. **Never remove always-on memory** — it runs at zero cost (Cloudflare Vectorize) and is the core differentiator
2. **Never lower the relevance threshold below 0.25** — below this, noise overwhelms the context
3. **Never raise MAX_RESULTS_TO_LLM above 30** — LLM context windows have limits
4. **Entity extraction must remain zero-cost** — regex-only, no LLM calls at capture time
5. **The intent gate still exists** for deep search — don't remove `_ms_intents` or `_vault_content_patterns`
6. **Always-on search failures are non-blocking** — wrapped in try/except, falls through to normal conversation
7. **Keep `_is_vault_share_text` check** — system-generated vault share text must not trigger memory search

## Patent Coverage

The existing provisional patent (`PATENT_SPLIT_SOVEREIGNTY_MEMORY.md`, filed March 2, 2026) covers the dual-store architecture and federated query delegation. The always-on semantic recall, multi-surface vector search, relevance-gated injection, and entity enrichment at capture are **new innovations not covered by the existing claims** — candidates for a continuation-in-part (CIP) filing.

## Verification After Changes

```bash
# Confirm Vectorize is configured
docker exec nate_bridge printenv | grep -i CF_

# Confirm always-on memory logs appear
docker logs nate_bridge --since 5m 2>&1 | grep "ALWAYS-ON MEMORY"

# Confirm entity extraction
docker exec nate_postgres psql -U nate_admin -d little_nate -c \
  "SELECT metadata->>'entities' FROM conversation_history WHERE metadata->>'entities' IS NOT NULL ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 3"
```
